in this lesson we're going to talk about  the median so what is the median well  the median basically gives you a sense  of the middle okay so when you think of  median think middle mean is the average  median is the middle so how do you find  the middle well if you have a list of  quantities or numbers you want to put  them in order from lowest to highest and  what you would do is you would count  like this towards the middle so in this  case we had an odd number of elements we  found that middle element and that's  going to be the median but what happens  if you have an even number of you know  quantities well look at this example  here we've got 3 and 12  then 4 and 10  and then when we get to the middle here  we have 6 and 8. so it's there's two in  the middle so what do we do well all we  do is we average them we add them  together and we divide by two so six  plus eight is fourteen divided by  divided by two is seven you can see  seven is right in the middle in between  those those two numbers so sometimes on  the act they might ask you a question  like you know what happens to the median  if you add  you know one number that's below the  median and one number that's above the  median well this would still be the same  middle number it wouldn't change but say  you added two numbers that were above  the median then it would shift the  median to the right if you had added two  numbers that were to the left of the  median then it would shift the median  you know lower to the left but if you're  adding the same number on both sides  it's going to keep the median the same  because that's still going to be the  middle number so just understanding this  concept of median and middle is  important let's go to this example see  if you can do this one so it says what  is the median height of the 15 students  listed in this histogram so you can see  here's the number of students one two  three four five and the given heights  here 61 60 inches through 65 inches is  the height  okay so pause the video see if you can  do that  and  what you would do is you'd say well  what's the middle of 15 well  that's going to be let's see right about  7 or 8 right so it's right there in the  middle it's going to be actually the  eighth student okay but when you look at  this you can see here's one student  here's two students that's three  students here's four more that's seven  the eighth student is going to be in  this block right here so it's going to  be a 63 inches is their height now if  you're not sure okay with that that  middle number here i'm just going to  show you one way you can write these out  there's not that many 10 11 12  13  14 15 so you can see 1 and 15 2 and 14 3  and 13 4 and 12 5 and 11 6 and 10  7 and 9 you can see 8 is that middle  number right so  8 is going to fall in this  interval right here so it looks like  that median height is 63 inches so  definitely an important concept to  understand i'll see you in the next  lesson
 

